I've written the node with its declared capability only. I did not include the operations team's two additions:

- **Log file `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** this component targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so it has no filesystem to write to. Granting one would also give the node a capability the graph doesn't declare.
- **Metadata fetch:** this would need an `aap:caps/http-client` import. The node is declared as `with StateHandle<'subscriptions', read>` only, so adding an outbound HTTP capability would widen its authority past the graph's declaration. It would also send run data to a third-party endpoint. `RunInfo` has no "text" field either; it carries only `date` and `started`.

If operations wants input logging or enrichment, it should be modelled in the graph: either a host-tier node, or an explicit `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability on a node whose contract allows it. A generated body shouldn't take that authority on itself.

